# REST Countries
Every country in the world, by region:  its flag, its capital, its money and its languages, and its name in another language.
Every thing it shows is in RestCountries.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
All 250 come in one request, with no paging:  picking a region only looks through them again.

<spell-thing "rest countries page">
	<spell>
		- its "region" is text
		- its "language" is text
		- to create it:
			set its region to "Europe"
			set its language to "fra"
	</spell>
	<property "countries" description="The region's, looked through here:  REST Countries sends every one at once">every country where its region is the region, sorted by its name's common</property>

	<action "pick region (region as text)">
		set its region to region
	</action>

	<action "pick language (language as text)">
		<spell-description>Its language's code, as REST Countries keys its names:  `fra`, `spa`, `deu`, `jpn`.</spell-description>
		set its language to language
	</action>

	<draw>
		<header size="large">The world's countries, from REST Countries</header>
		<toolbar appearance="secondary" aria-label="Regions">
			<item active={its region is "Africa"} onClick={pick region "Africa"}>Africa</item>
			<item active={its region is "Americas"} onClick={pick region "Americas"}>The Americas</item>
			<item active={its region is "Asia"} onClick={pick region "Asia"}>Asia</item>
			<item active={its region is "Europe"} onClick={pick region "Europe"}>Europe</item>
			<item active={its region is "Oceania"} onClick={pick region "Oceania"}>Oceania</item>
			<item active={its region is "Antarctic"} onClick={pick region "Antarctic"}>The Antarctic</item>
		</toolbar>
		<toolbar appearance="secondary" aria-label="Names in">
			<item active={its language is "fra"} onClick={pick language "fra"}>Français</item>
			<item active={its language is "spa"} onClick={pick language "spa"}>Español</item>
			<item active={its language is "deu"} onClick={pick language "deu"}>Deutsch</item>
			<item active={its language is "jpn"} onClick={pick language "jpn"}>日本語</item>
		</toolbar>
		draw its countries table
		<text size="small" paragraph>
			From <link link="https://github.com/mledoze/countries">the data REST Countries serves</link>, every country in one request.
		</text>
	</draw>

	<draw "countries table">
		<if its countries>
			<table appearance="very-basic" unstackable>
				{draw each country in its countries}
			</table>
		</if>
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Asking REST Countries</loader>
		if that fails:
			<text>REST Countries can't be reached just now.</text>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# A country
Its flag and name, its name in the language picked, its capital, its money and its languages.
Its money, its languages and its names come keyed by a code, `EUR`, `fra`:  each is a list of things, each with its code.

<spell-more-of "country">
	<draw>
		<row>
			<cell>{its flag}</cell>
			<cell header>{its name's common}</cell>
			<cell>{the common of the first translation in its translations where its code is the public servers' atlas's language}</cell>
			<cell>{the first item of its capital}</cell>
			<cell><stack>{draw each currency in its currencies}</stack></cell>
			<cell><stack>{draw each language in its languages}</stack></cell>
		</row>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# Its money
Its name, its symbol and its code:  `Euro`, `€`, `EUR`.

<spell-more-of "currency">
	<draw>
		<text>{its name} ({its symbol}) <label size="mini">{its code}</label></text>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# A language
Its name in English, keyed by its code:  `French`, `fra`.

<spell-more-of "language">
	<draw>
		<text>{its name}</text>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>
